    {
      "id": "file:src/main.cpp",
      "type": "file",
      "name": "main.cpp",
      "filePath": "src/main.cpp",
      "summary": "Application entry point for the CoreStationHXAgent; bootstraps the platform abstraction, manages serial communication and heartbeat threads, handles AMT COM port detection/reassignment via the Windows registry, and relays system state to the CoreStation HX CMC over serial.",
      "tags": ["entry-point", "service", "serial-communication", "windows-registry", "multithreading"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Heavy use of Windows-specific APIs (RegOpenKeyExW, WMI-adjacent includes) guarded by #ifdef _WIN32, combined with cross-platform serial/platform abstractions; runs heartbeat and serial polling on separate std::thread workers synchronized via atomics and a mutex-protected SystemState."
    },
    {
